{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he bowed.</b> I do not know who bowed to whom, when it says 'איש לרעהו' — who is called 'איש'? This is Moses, as it is said: 'איש האלהים'. But this is difficult, for Jethro too is called 'איש', as it is said: 'ויואל משה לשבת את האיש' etc. One may answer: we derive 'איש' from 'איש', but we do not derive 'איש' from 'האיש'. Another answer: Moses is called 'איש' adjacent to his name, as it is said: 'והאיש משה' — unlike Jethro. Another answer: this derashah follows the one who says that Reuel was Jethro's father, and what is written 'ויתן לו את צפורה בתו לאשה' — it means his son's daughter, for grandchildren are considered like children."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:22.353294636Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}